From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jayweihung <3034830+jayweihung@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:39:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] feat: hc send --queue --key holds a message until the
 program stops working

The core types it in once the terminal is no longer working or blocked (one
entry per key; queuing the key again replaces it) and keeps it as sent until
the turn it started ends, in the record's queued list with a queued event, so
every panel can show the same compacting state. A program that never reports
status gets it at once.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
